#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# maximize

#% text
# `maximize(f, x)` gives the global maximum of `f` over the reals as `[value, [x -> point]]`; `maximize([f, cond], x)` under a condition.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is computed as `minimize` of `-f`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A quartic with two maxima:

#% cell
maximize(-x^4 + 2*x^2, x)
#% output
#= [1, [x -> -1]]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# On an interval:

#% cell
maximize([x*(1 - x), 0 <= x and x <= 1], x)
#% output
#= [1/4, [x -> 1/2]]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The value alone:

#% cell
max_value([x*(1 - x), 0 <= x and x <= 1], x)
#% output
#= 1/4

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `minimize`, `max_value`, `arg_max`
